@startuml unify-ocr-layout-workflow

title Unify - OCR, Layout Detection & Reading Order

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

start

:Receive DocumentMetadata\n(from Prepare-Doc) +\noriginal/preprocessed file;

if ("DocumentMetadata.error_state?") then (Yes)
  :Return passthrough error\nas OCRDocument;
  stop
else (No)
endif

:Determine OCR strategy\nfrom:\n- pdf_type\n- DQS / IQA metrics\n- has_text flags\n- ocr_routing_recommendation;

partition "Per-page routing" {
  if ("Page has_text == false") then (Yes)
    :Skip heavy OCR.\nFlag as image_only;\nRun layout detection without\nOCR text spans;
  else (No)
    :Run primary OCR engine\n(RapidOCR — fast, Docling-integrated)\nwith layout awareness;
    :Run secondary OCR engine(s)\n(EasyOCR — fallback for hard images,\nnon-Latin scripts);
    :Optionally run fast OCR\n(Tesseract — third-tier baseline);
  endif
}

partition "Layout & structure" {
  note right #FFF3E0
    **Scope Note:**
    Coarse layout detection (11 DocLayNet classes) is performed
    upstream by Prepare-Doc and provided in DocumentMetadata.json.
    Unify performs full reading order + table structure analysis only.
    Source: docs/architecture/diagrams/level-2/downstream-context/index.md
  end note
  :Consume coarse layout\nfrom Prepare-Doc\n(DocumentMetadata.json);

  :Attach text spans from OCR\ninto LayoutElements\n(using bounding box overlap);

  :Run table structure model\n(PubTables-1M / ClusterTabNet)\nfor Table elements;

  :Detect parasitic content\n(headers, footers, watermarks)\n& mark is_parasitic=true;

  :Detect specialized regions:\n- Formula\n- Handwriting\n- Signatures / stamps\n- Margin notes;
}

partition "Reading order & links" {
  :Compute reading_order sequence\nfrom layout graph\n(graph-based spatial reasoning);

  :Link captions to figures;\nlink footnotes to markers;

  :Attach page-level\nreading_order_confidence\nand layout_type\n(single vs multi-column);
}

:Assemble OCRDocument:\n- per-page LayoutElements\n- engine-wise text + confidence\n- reading_order chains\n- table structures\n- parasitic flags\n- specialized regions;

:Emit OCRDocument\n(to Chunk);

stop

note right
  **CONTEXT DIAGRAM**
  This diagram shows the downstream Unify project's workflow.
  It is provided here to illustrate how Prepare-Doc outputs
  (DocumentMetadata.json + corrected images) are consumed.
  Unify internals are NOT part of the Prepare-Doc codebase.

  **Prepare-Doc Outputs Consumed:**
  - DocumentMetadata.json (DQS, IQA metrics, routing recommendation)
  - Corrected page images (deskewed, enhanced)
  - Coarse layout detections (11 DocLayNet classes)

  **Documentation:**
  [[docs/development/RAG Pipeline/ingest-prepare-doc-contract.md]]
  [[docs/development/RAG Pipeline/prepare-doc-unify-contract.md]]
  [[docs/architecture/diagrams/level-2/downstream-context/index.md]]

  **ADR:**
  [[docs/ADRs/0029-prepare-doc-scope-boundaries.md]]
end note


